From c57b0d155a7ba3ec75766cf49d62df12b49c83e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 18:17:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 043/113] media: qcom: camss: add support for the MSM8998 CAMSS

MSM8998 is SDM660's CAMSS: CSID v5.0, ISPIF v3.0 and VFE 4.8 sit at the
same offsets and answer to the same programming, so the whole of it comes
down to resource tables and the already upstream csid_ops_4_7,
ispif/vfe_ops_4_8 and csiphy_ops_3ph_1_0.

The CSIPHY is the one part that differs. It is a v5.0.1 2-phase PHY, so it
takes the generic gen2 path with a lane register table of its own rather
than the gen1 sequence SDM660 uses, and it has a core clock the older PHYs
do not - left at its power-on default the PHY cannot sample a high speed
link, and says nothing about it.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
